      <p><strong>Cleaning companies in Nepal can schedule crews and track jobs by giving every job a date, time, site and named staff, letting customers book themselves, and recording status and payment per job. Zennly refuses to book the same person twice at the same time.</strong></p>

<p>A cleaning business succeeds or fails on logistics: the right people at the right address at the right time, every day. Most companies start by managing this on phone calls and group chats, which works for a handful of jobs and breaks well before you reach a dozen.</p>
<h2>The usual problems</h2>
<ul>
<li>A crew is promised to two sites at once.</li>
<li>A customer books by phone and the job never reaches the crew.</li>
<li>Nobody is sure whether a job was finished, or paid for.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Schedule staff to jobs, not just days</h2>
<p>Each job needs a date, a time, a site and named staff. A scheduling system that attaches staff to jobs &ndash; and refuses to book the same person twice at the same time &ndash; removes most of the confusion.</p>
<h2>Give customers a way to book</h2>
<p>Let customers choose a service and a time themselves and get a booking number back. Your office then handles exceptions instead of taking every order by phone.</p>
<h2>Track status through the day</h2>
<p>Marking each job as it progresses &ndash; booked, in progress, done &ndash; gives the office a live picture, without calling crews for updates.</p>
<h2>Record payment per job</h2>
<p>Note what was paid, and how, against each job. At the end of the day the totals are already there. <a href="/solutions/cleaning/">See how Zennly works for cleaning companies</a>.</p>

      <h2>Cleaning service scheduling in Nepal: what helps first</h2>
      <p>Many cleaning companies in Nepal take orders by phone and message. Start by putting every job in one schedule with the crew attached, then let customers book a service and time themselves. Record payment per job so the end-of-day total is already correct.</p>

      <h2>Common questions</h2>
      <h3>How can a cleaning company in Nepal schedule crews?</h3>
      <p>Attach named staff to each job with a date, time and site in a scheduling system that refuses to book the same person twice at once.</p>
      <h3>How do cleaning companies track whether a job is done and paid?</h3>
      <p>Mark each job as booked, in progress or done, and record what was paid and how against the job.</p>

